    {
      "id": "ES-C409-fin-de-semana",
      "sequence": 9300,
      "title": "el fin de semana — the week's end",
      "headword": "el fin de semana",
      "romanization": "el fin de semana",
      "gloss": "the weekend",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:94250624be62f894",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Spanish builds “weekend” as a transparent phrase: el fin de semana, literally “the end of the week.” It gives a time for a plan: voy a preparar el postre este fin de semana."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The phrase, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fin continues Latin fīnis, “boundary” or “end.” Semana continues Late Latin septimāna, the seven-day period. The little de joins them: fin de semana. Learn the three words as one planning block."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: one weekend, many weekends",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For one, say el fin de semana. In the plural, only the first noun changes: los fines de semana. For a regular habit, trabajo los fines de semana; for one upcoming period, este fin de semana."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "el fin de semana",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *el fin de semana*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "este fin de semana",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *este fin de semana*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "los fines de semana",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *los fines de semana*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The weekend? (El fin de semana.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sources: DLE: fin; DLE: semana."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C409-reservar",
      "sequence": 9310,
      "title": "reservar — set it aside",
      "headword": "reservar",
      "romanization": "reservar",
      "gloss": "to reserve, to book",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:38bfbd41f5bf202a",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have chosen el fin de semana. To book a room for it, use reservar: reservar una habitación."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin reservāre meant “keep back” or “preserve.” That image still works: a hotel sets a room aside for you. English reserve is a close relative. Keep the history at that safe level; resemblance to servir is not a reason to invent a separate family story."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: book a thing for people",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The thing follows directly: reservar una habitación. Add the people with para: para dos personas. Together: quiero reservar una habitación para dos personas."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "reservar",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *reservar*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "reservar una habitación",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *reservar una habitación*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "para dos personas",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *para dos personas*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To reserve or book? (Reservar.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: DLE: reservar."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C409-incluir",
      "sequence": 9320,
      "title": "incluir — close it inside the whole",
      "headword": "incluir",
      "romanization": "incluir",
      "gloss": "to include",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:dee06aa9bbef6f55",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can reservar a room. Now ask what comes inside the price: ¿Incluye el desayuno?, “Does it include breakfast?”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Spanish borrowed incluir from Latin inclūdere, literally “close in”: in, “in,” plus claudere, “close.” English include, exclude and conclude share the same learned family. Something included is enclosed inside the whole."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the useful third-person form",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The infinitive is incluir, but hotel messages often use incluye: el precio incluye el desayuno. In a question, keep the same form and lift the intonation: ¿Incluye el desayuno?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "incluir",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *incluir*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "incluye el desayuno",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *incluye el desayuno*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "el precio incluye el desayuno",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *el precio incluye el desayuno*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To include? (Incluir.) Does it include breakfast? (¿Incluye el desayuno?)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: DLE: incluir."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
